-- title:
--   Localising at powers of r: finite free faithfully flat algebras over S_{gr}
-- statement:
--   Let $S$ be a commutative ring and let $g, r \in S$. Let $C$ be a commutative ring carrying an $S$-algebra structure and an algebra structure over the localisation $S_g =$ `Localization.Away g`, the two being compatible in the sense that $S \to S_g \to C$ is a tower of scalars, and assume that $C$ is finite and free as an $S_g$-module, faithfully flat over $S_g$, and of finite presentation as an $S_g$-algebra. Let $C'$ be a commutative ring which is simultaneously an $S$-algebra and a $C$-algebra, with $S \to C \to C'$ a tower of scalars, and assume that $C'$ is a localisation of $C$ at the submonoid `Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid C (Submonoid.powers r)` generated by the image in $C$ of the powers of $r$. The conclusion asserts the existence of an algebra structure on $C'$ over $S_{gr} =$ `Localization.Away (g * r)` together with a compatibility making $S \to S_{gr} \to C'$ a tower of scalars, for which $C'$ is finite and free as an $S_{gr}$-module, faithfully flat over $S_{gr}$, and of finite presentation as an $S_{gr}$-algebra.
--
--   This is the standard patching step saying that the four properties of being finite, free, faithfully flat and of finite presentation for an algebra over a basic open $\operatorname{Spec} S_g$ persist after shrinking the base to the smaller basic open $\operatorname{Spec} S_{gr}$, the algebra being replaced by its localisation at the powers of $r$. It is used in the construction of auxiliary finite faithfully flat covers in the study of good reduction of Jacobians, where an open set has to be shrunk so as to avoid a prescribed prime.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Algebra_exists_algebra_away_mul_finite_free_faithfullyFlat_finitePresentation_of_isLocalization_powers.lean

